If the previous MenuProps override still isn't forcing the menu to avoid the taskbar, it is because MUI's underlying Popover component (which <Select> uses) can sometimes fail to correctly calculate the window boundaries when new rows are dynamically added to the very bottom of the DOM.
Here are the two best ways to fix this permanently so it never gets cut off again:
### Option 1: Force the Menu to Open Upwards (Drop-up)
If you want to keep using the current TextField select, we can strictly invert the origin points. This tells MUI to never attempt to open downwards, forcing the menu to always render **above** the input field where there is plenty of screen space.
```jsx
{/* Currency */}
<Grid item size={{ xl: 1.5, lg: 2 }}>
  <TextField
    select 
    fullWidth
    label="Currency *" 
    value={row.currency} 
    InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
    onChange={(e) => { 
      handleRowChange(row.id, "currency", e.target.value); 
      handleRowChange(row.id, "amount", ""); 
    }}
    SelectProps={{
      displayEmpty: true,
      renderValue: (selected) => !selected ? <span style={{ color: 'gray', opacity: 0.8 }}>Select Currency</span> : selected,
      MenuProps: {
        PaperProps: { 
          style: { maxHeight: 220 } 
        },
        // FORCES the menu to always open upwards from the top edge
        anchorOrigin: {
          vertical: 'top',
          horizontal: 'left',
        },
        transformOrigin: {
          vertical: 'bottom',
          horizontal: 'left',
        }
      }
    }}
  >
    {currencyOptions.map((c) => (<MenuItem key={c} value={c}>{c}</MenuItem>))}
  </TextField>
</Grid>

```
### Option 2: Convert to Autocomplete (Highly Recommended)
Because your **Branch** and **CGL** fields already use <Autocomplete>, replacing the Currency <Select> with an <Autocomplete> will make your UI code consistent. More importantly, <Autocomplete> uses a different positioning engine (Popper.js), which is significantly smarter at detecting screen edges and flipping the menu automatically than the older Popover engine used by <Select>.
```jsx
{/* Currency */}
<Grid item size={{ xl: 1.5, lg: 2 }}>
  <Autocomplete
    disableClearable
    options={currencyOptions}
    value={row.currency || null}
    onChange={(event, newValue) => {
      handleRowChange(row.id, "currency", newValue || "");
      handleRowChange(row.id, "amount", "");
    }}
    // Popper automatically flips based on available screen space
    slotProps={{
      popper: {
        modifiers: [
          { name: 'flip', enabled: true },
          { name: 'preventOverflow', enabled: true }
        ]
      }
    }}
    renderInput={(params) => (
      <TextField
        {...params}
        label="Currency *"
        placeholder={!row.currency ? "Select Currency" : ""}
        InputLabelProps={{ shrink: true }}
      />
    )}
  />
</Grid>

```
